  "body": "A new command available during a heartbeat: **`Heart.schedule_pulse(reason, after=N | at=K)`** (+ `scheduled()` / `cancel_pulse()`, and `AppAIRuntime.schedule_pulse` for the MIND).\n\nThe organism plans a wake on a **future beat** \u2014 a countdown or a scheduled beat \u2014 so it can **chain a thought** to a later pulse and run a task only as often as it really needs, staying **asleep (event-gated)** until the due beat. It's the *later* companion to nociception's `pain` (*now*); the woken snapshot carries `scheduled: True`. Planning is measured in **beats** (the organism's native unit of time).\n\n- `mantle/organs/heart.py`: the `_schedule` queue + `schedule_pulse`/`scheduled`/`cancel_pulse`, wired into `beat()` so a due wake rides the existing event-gated path; contract updated.\n- `mantle/mind/runtime.py`: `schedule_pulse` / `scheduled_pulses` passthrough.\n- `audits/invariants.py`: **SCHED-1** (a scheduled pulse wakes on the due beat and not before; one-shot). Count **66 \u2192 67**; README/FIELD_GUIDE/Part-1/2 docs updated; the `doctor` docs-vs-code gate stays green.\n- `teach.py` + `FIELD_GUIDE.md`: chapter **\"Planning Ahead\"** (proven live \u2014 teach 17/17); Part 2 \u00a72.6 documents it.\n- Examples (MacroDroid YAML `gen4_capabilities` + both HTML demos' system prompts) describe the command. *Functional in-browser wiring is deferred to the demo rebuild.*\n- `docs/MOLT_LEDGER.md`: logged as a post-merge addition; net 36 \u2192 67.\n\n**67/67 invariants green; Stage-1 + Stage-2 pass; tamper proofs still catch; teach 17/17.**\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
